  "Question": "Describe the opening direction, vertex, and axis of symmetry of \\(y=-2x^2\\). Which of the following is correct?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "Opens upward, vertex \\((0,0)\\), axis of symmetry is the \\(x\\)-axis",
    "B": "Opens downward, vertex \\((0,0)\\), axis of symmetry is the \\(y\\)-axis",
    "C": "Opens downward, vertex \\((0,-2)\\), axis of symmetry is the \\(y\\)-axis",
    "D": "Opens upward, vertex \\((0,0)\\), axis of symmetry is the \\(y\\)-axis"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\(a=-2<0\\), so the parabola opens downward. The vertex of \\(y=ax^2\\) is at the origin \\((0,0)\\), and its axis of symmetry is the \\(y\\)-axis.",
